#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105596 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "b3be2b13-b455-5dde-accf-259c075e1e1f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4350" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105597 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/id #uuid "c6f2dacc-11b0-5689-97d9-e1869c64aae1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4351" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105598 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "4deee6cc-69e4-5da4-9c78-57bf6c988500" :question/math-academy-id "e-4352" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262894 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "002fdf74-6f71-54b2-830e-d9c31f46d601" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259874} {:answer/id #uuid "2aca00cd-0b17-53b6-983e-a2657da0646e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260251} {:answer/id #uuid "700a04d5-9011-5132-bdd4-e0be0859896c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260858} {:answer/id #uuid "a765a9d3-1a6b-59c4-8235-ac04896438b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261337} {:answer/id #uuid "c020a971-5df5-5817-a759-23a1a56b9b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c020a971-5df5-5817-a759-23a1a56b9b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261573} :answer-field/id #uuid "22e9d0a6-6a14-5045-961e-92c3a61748d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28e94f1b-b25a-5f14-a6d0-bd87b063c727" :question/math-academy-id "q-128436" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨8,0,3⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,1,1⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 3)-(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 3)+4(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-3k+1+32 \\\\  & =33-3k \\\\  & =3(11-k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 3(11-k) & =0 \\\\ 11-k & =0 \\\\ k & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "416f2b02-f671-5dac-9033-c92a97bb7433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285396} {:answer/id #uuid "66d33b0d-7ab1-5eac-8f4e-3d2df7928766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285722} {:answer/id #uuid "e258b1f3-74dd-5a16-b9ea-949bbeba773d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286849} {:answer/id #uuid "e508fab7-8c7c-5655-84d6-97881cdb4aae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286884} {:answer/id #uuid "e5eaf3c4-9cd2-569f-bb87-a49a632e2001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66d33b0d-7ab1-5eac-8f4e-3d2df7928766" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285722} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf368173-4107-5226-9931-f9efe2d03ed0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2a99499-e25e-5c3a-b8fd-38e4eb5f4e8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-18259" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-3,3,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,3⟩$ and $c=⟨0,4,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3((-1)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)+(2\\cdot 4-0\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =39-6+8 \\\\  & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|41|=41.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030d4dbf-31a4-5c0b-ac81-fba854373f33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458621} {:answer/id #uuid "73574c6b-9bf8-53da-8eb4-4206538d870d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458830} {:answer/id #uuid "9f870293-8ab2-51ce-aeed-f745f0ba194c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458911} {:answer/id #uuid "beb8454a-c986-5919-9b86-28dfc102e89c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458970} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c4fd6b-08ec-58ae-80a4-d8e5d351c013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4c4fd6b-08ec-58ae-80a4-d8e5d351c013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459025} :answer-field/id #uuid "70ec86a9-e96a-54b6-bdab-92b2a2a8c0ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f94fb95c-1aca-535d-ab25-0d9749d43fb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-18262" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, $q=⟨-2,3,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-1,4,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-((-2)\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 1)-((-2)\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+5 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b91b1ff-04f2-5241-991f-a0cc2cfb0602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284879} {:answer/id #uuid "5c7e0a12-c398-51c0-ac5a-185f2ba8acab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285635} {:answer/id #uuid "7171ef21-9125-54d8-8548-7452920c7a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285829} {:answer/id #uuid "af7840a2-d107-597a-a2b9-cc938cae9f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286386} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5d05e0-fae6-5640-bc73-d08f6f6d4a87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7171ef21-9125-54d8-8548-7452920c7a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285829} :answer-field/id #uuid "62967656-4da8-539f-8bc8-d9d85e319b59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1d7560d3-4e5c-58e1-a4ce-975d4218030d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20145" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(2,1,2)$, $B(3,3,3)$, $C(-2,-1,3)$, and $D(4,1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+3j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+j+4k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 1)-2((-4)\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1)+((-4)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-4+20+4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|20|=20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd4b21f5-ae4e-533c-a49c-e215e4954375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd4b21f5-ae4e-533c-a49c-e215e4954375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572528} :answer-field/id #uuid "752eecbd-7383-564b-9c0e-74b4d04c57f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "02e4dd76-291f-501d-9dd9-df687e45b52b" :question/math-academy-id "q-280320" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(0,2,-1),$ $B(3,4,1),$ $C(-1,3,2),$ and $D(2,1,0).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+k)-(2j-k) \\\\  & =3i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+3j+2k)-(2j-k) \\\\  & =-i+j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(2j-k) \\\\  & =2i-j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1))-2((-1)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2)+2((-1)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3(1+3)-2(-1-6)+2(1-2) \\\\  & =12-(-14)-2 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|24|=24.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35b3feda-548d-5212-bb14-ab63c3adb049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35b3feda-548d-5212-bb14-ab63c3adb049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293161} :answer-field/id #uuid "3654f79e-6420-50ab-9f46-330c40c4756d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "783ca205-66c5-547b-848c-076696d6e4cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-280712" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,5,0⟩$, and $c=⟨4,0,6⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(30)-2(0)+3(-20) \\\\  & =30-0-60 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-30|=30.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d46a7ab-4f0b-5721-bebb-a49f4264e23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d46a7ab-4f0b-5721-bebb-a49f4264e23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572453} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ef8f1ee-ea2b-53fa-8813-6530aca61521" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c885246f-c4a6-5da3-b8cb-28ee3dc779d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-280713" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $x=⟨2,3,0⟩$, $y=⟨1,4,5⟩$, and $z=⟨0,2,6⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 6-5\\cdot 2)-3(1\\cdot 6-5\\cdot 0)+0 \\\\  & =2(24-10)-3(6) \\\\  & =28-18 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad103bee-c9bb-538f-b95a-de0c98d63213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad103bee-c9bb-538f-b95a-de0c98d63213" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572503} :answer-field/id #uuid "2566d49a-718e-5a8c-9b71-cc6e6ef2e3db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "443a4021-2ecb-5b8a-948d-b71804528fab" :question/math-academy-id "q-280715" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $p=⟨1,0,5⟩$, $q=⟨3,2,6⟩$, and $r=⟨0,4,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(2\\cdot 1-6\\cdot 4)+0+5(3\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-22+60 \\\\  & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|38|=38.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2dab13-46de-5120-87e8-8117a287ba97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c2dab13-46de-5120-87e8-8117a287ba97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293049} :answer-field/id #uuid "89673c8b-815d-53a8-b014-fbcc596ce325" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee4f8503-0b7f-5200-9b9f-9ac97e166c2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280729" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,k,k⟩$, $b=⟨0,3,2⟩$, and $c=⟨4,0,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & k & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|-k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(3\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 0)-k(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 4)+k(0\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =15+8k-12k \\\\  & =15-4k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 15-4k & =0 \\\\ 4k & =15 \\\\ k & =\\frac{15}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{15}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572726 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efac262e-978f-52d8-b514-d218c8e2aaf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efac262e-978f-52d8-b514-d218c8e2aaf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572579} :answer-field/id #uuid "2170e711-c9bf-56cc-a436-de505690692b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572599}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef51444c-d286-591b-9ba9-aedca70d62d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-280746" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,k,2⟩$, $b=⟨1,3,0⟩$, and $c=⟨0,4,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}k & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k(3\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 4)-k(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 0)+2(1\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =k(15)-k(5)+2(4) \\\\  & =15k-5k+8 \\\\  & =10k+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 10k+8 & =0 \\\\ 10k & =-8 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{4}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8801f3a-9dfd-5e9f-8521-78d48c05cc43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8801f3a-9dfd-5e9f-8521-78d48c05cc43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293652} :answer-field/id #uuid "57b4cf71-7bea-51e2-9884-e3e9016b64cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35b9e288-8b36-5336-a7cf-8f490e426c0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-281023" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,0,2),$ $B(3,4,5),$ $C(6,2,4),$ and $D(5,3,6).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+5k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =2i+4j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,4,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(6i+2j+4k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =5i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨5,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(5i+3j+6k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =4i+3j+4k \\\\  & =⟨4,3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 3)-4(5\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 4)+3(5\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2(8-6)-4(20-8)+3(15-8) \\\\  & =4-48+21 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-23|=23.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295175 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7cb7e495-32de-5ba1-b91b-cfaa604be24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cb7e495-32de-5ba1-b91b-cfaa604be24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293432} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaec393b-7696-58c0-adfd-28a0339820a5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7ad6a5b8-f3d8-5275-887d-fa59251ace92" :question/math-academy-id "q-281029" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(0,1,3),$ $B(0,5,5),$ $C(3,4,5),$ and $D(2,0,2).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5j+5k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =4j+2k \\\\  & =⟨0,4,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+5k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =3i+3j+2k \\\\  & =⟨3,3,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+2k)-(1j+3k) \\\\  & =2i-1j-1k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4(3\\cdot -1-2\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot -1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =28-18 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326925 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09532a7b-1bde-5425-aa2a-a897fa63b438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324054} {:answer/id #uuid "2c6d850b-f14f-5354-8f2a-89eb6f418867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324329} {:answer/id #uuid "88ce51b5-6b4e-5a60-90fa-8279e2abd028" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325135} {:answer/id #uuid "9a93b40d-5533-56f2-bb93-1c0e463a14c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325288} {:answer/id #uuid "cd846ac4-5a9b-5d65-b3ce-525881f5605f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd846ac4-5a9b-5d65-b3ce-525881f5605f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325756} :answer-field/id #uuid "105ffdf3-9def-5878-8052-550f2e45a407" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326250}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6db83569-7cb0-5537-ab90-423f6f08147e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42048" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,2,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $c=⟨4,1,3⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)-2(3\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-2k-2+6 \\\\  & =-2k+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -2k+4 & =0 \\\\ 2k & =4 \\\\ k & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "480d8a6c-d976-500e-a7e2-36b07adb1298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339770} {:answer/id #uuid "92b3ca28-cec3-54f5-8108-604c09001fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340447} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ccd3d8-500a-5a10-b8dd-140f303da80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340777} {:answer/id #uuid "c7936625-73aa-5282-9707-cfefef43ada2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340898} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ddbf57-82d0-56ba-af3f-5120ce6bc488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5ccd3d8-500a-5a10-b8dd-140f303da80d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340777} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9dc32f6-3810-5869-9997-de4c6edc03fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "029d2415-156a-588b-85c8-9df58fb943a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-73736" :question/problem "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨t,1,t⟩$, $q=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and $r=⟨3,0,1⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}t & 1 & t \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t((-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-1))-(2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1))+t(2\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-t-5+3t \\\\  & =2t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 2t-5 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =5 \\\\ t & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=\\frac{5}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342076 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Position Vectors Given Their Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40d26a0c-7c01-5b6a-8dbe-ae3604c79b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339707} {:answer/id #uuid "a94320ec-b8fb-55d4-958d-7f0d1f959771" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340668} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f68538-632a-565b-b512-ff8470d73e8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341125} {:answer/id #uuid "e65f7298-4237-5dfe-b5fe-c41469fbc270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341164} {:answer/id #uuid "f379ed93-ced2-52c2-a4c4-17422c45cfea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40d26a0c-7c01-5b6a-8dbe-ae3604c79b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339707} :answer-field/id #uuid "96aeb4dc-4ea9-539b-be68-45022f3c1e44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d447f611-67a9-5187-a844-7f81dc30a0cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-73745" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,-1,2)$, $B(-2,2,3)$, $C(1,1,1)$, and $D(-1,3,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+2j+3k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j+k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-i+3j-2k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+4j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-2,4,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot (-4)-4\\cdot (-1))-3(0\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot (-1))+(0\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12+6+4 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|22|=22.\n$$"}]}
